From 4265fed3ea042711e270fbb902fc5a7575964f1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:06:06 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 239/404] Unified: AI chat works on Windows and behind a
 company proxy; network and AI chat preferences
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Windows bundle: do not replace Lib/ssl.py with package/bundle/windows/ssl-patch.py.
  It is the ssl.py of Python 3.11 and imports RAND_pseudo_bytes, which the bundled
  Python 3.13's _ssl no longer has, so 'import ssl' failed everywhere and the AI chat
  stopped with "cannot import name 'RAND_pseudo_bytes' from '_ssl'". Its workaround
  (skip a bad certificate in the Windows store) is built into Python 3.10+.
- Edit → Preferences → General → Network (new, app-wide): proxy (system settings by
  default / none / manual, with exceptions) and the company's certificate file for
  networks that inspect TLS. Applied to the environment at startup and on save
  (HTTPS_PROXY, HTTP_PROXY, NO_PROXY, SSL_CERT_FILE, REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE,
  NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS) so Python, the AI chat bridge and claude use it, and to Qt's
  application proxy. With the system setting, the Windows proxy (Internet Options,
  with its exceptions) is turned into these variables, since claude reads only them.
- Edit → Preferences → General → AI chat (new): change or remove the API key. The
  panel no longer has a permanent "API key…" button; "Enter the API key…" appears only
  when a key is needed.
- AI chat: a proxy or certificate error is explained in Japanese with where to fix
  it; while claude retries a failed connection the panel says so instead of waiting
  silently.
- AIAgentBridge --self-test: loads ssl, claude-agent-sdk and the bundled claude
  without connecting; the Windows and Linux bundles run it and fail if it does not
  pass. --has-key for the preferences page.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
